# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env* files are gitignored; this example is not.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  CLIENT (safe to expose — Vite inlines every VITE_ variable into the
#  bundle that ships to the browser, so never put a secret here)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Path (or absolute URL) of the backend explanation route.
# Leave unset to keep answering from the local mock catalog.
# VITE_EXPLANATION_API_URL=/api/explain


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  SERVER (never exposed to the browser — read only by backend code)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The backend route does not exist yet. When it does, its LLM credential is
# read here, server-side, and never forwarded to the client. No VITE_ prefix:
# that prefix is exactly what would publish it.
#
# LLM_API_KEY=
